hint: Loop while both pointers are inside their lists.
hint: Equal front items: append one and move both pointers. Otherwise move the pointer at the smaller item, which can't match anything further along the other list.
hint: Searching the other list with `in` for every item would be O(n²).
right: Each step moves at least one pointer, so the walk takes at most len(a) + len(b) steps: O(n), like merge.
wrong: Walk i along a and j along b. When `a[i] == b[j]`, keep it and move both; when `a[i] < b[j]`, move i; otherwise move j.

