fail[3]: Every pair is in the wrong order: 6.
fail[5]: Each 2 is before the 1: 2. Equal items aren't an inversion.
fail[6]: 3–2, 3–1, 2–1 and the second 3–1: 4.
hint: Each call returns two things: `left, a = sort_count(items[:mid])`.
hint: Start the count at `a + b`, the inversions inside each half.
hint: In the merge, when `right[j]` is taken, add `len(left) - i`. Use `<=`, so equal items aren't counted.
right: Inversions inside each half are counted by the recursive calls, and the ones between the halves all at once during the merge. Checking every pair would be O(n²).
wrong: Merge sort the list, and whenever the merge takes an item from the right half, add the number of left items still waiting, `len(left) - i`: each of those is bigger and came earlier.

