title: Merge sort without recursion
prompt: Merge sort can also work **bottom-up**, without recursion. Start with width 1: merge each pair of neighbouring runs of 1 item, then each pair of runs of 2 items, then 4, doubling the width until one run covers the whole list. Write `merge_sort_bottom_up(items)` that returns a new sorted list this way. `merge` is given. The speed check uses lists in reverse order.
starter:
```python
def merge(left, right):
    merged = []
    i = 0
    j = 0
    while i < len(left) and j < len(right):
        if left[i] <= right[j]:
            merged.append(left[i])
            i += 1
        else:
            merged.append(right[j])
